    "title": {
      "en": "be, have, and asking questions",
      "fr": "be, have, et poser des questions"
    },
    "steps": [
      {
        "en": "BE: I am, you are, he / she / it is, we are, you are, they are. HAVE: he / she / it has, everyone else have. Age uses BE: I am ten. Questions turn BE round: Are you ready? Is she French? One thing: there is; several: there are.",
        "fr": "BE : I am, you are, he / she / it is, we are, you are, they are. HAVE : he / she / it has, tous les autres have. L’âge se dit avec BE : I am ten. La question inverse BE : Are you ready? Is she French? Une chose : there is ; plusieurs : there are."
      },
      {
        "en": "Question words: what (quoi), where (où), when (quand), who (qui), why (pourquoi), how (comment); how old, how many. Irregular past: learn the pairs, go / went, see / saw, eat / ate.",
        "fr": "Les mots interrogatifs : what (quoi), where (où), when (quand), who (qui), why (pourquoi), how (comment) ; how old, how many. Le prétérit irrégulier : apprends les paires, go / went, see / saw, eat / ate."
